item 1 barrier is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/1/barrier".

item 1 barrier is an assessment statement.

item 1 barrier has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationNegative".

item 1 barrier has the judgement "-Agreements on additional quality checks, confidentiality requirements, and dissemination of the ECR data, are to beestablishedbetween theCommission and the MemberStates".

item 1 barrier has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeAlignmentBarrier".

item 1 barrier concerns the service interop 1.

item 1 barrier has the description "Assess the alignment with existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified".


item 1 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/1/measure".

item 1 measure is an assessment statement.

item 1 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 1 measure has the judgement "This act ensures consistency and streamlines statistical processes in the area of European fisheries and aquaculture statistics.
Under the legal framework of Regulation (EC) No 223/2009.
Relying on data (Council Regulation (EC) No 1224/2009 of the European Parliament and of the Council and Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2017/218 of 6 February 2017),
Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2017/218.
Aligned with the DCF (Regulation (EU) No 2017/1004).".

item 1 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeAlignmentMeasure".

item 1 measure concerns the service interop 1.

item 1 measure has the description "Assess the alignment with existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified".


item 2 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/2/measure".

item 2 measure is an assessment statement.

item 2 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 2 measure has the judgement "-Asis the case forall European statistics disseminated by Eurostat,fisheries and aquaculture statistics are associated with ametadata description; - Member Statesare advisedto use the‘latest version of the SIMS’(see Commission Recommendation (EU) 2023/397). All tables disseminated by Eurostat are associated with ametadata description.
-Uses the existing network of statistical offices.".

item 2 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeOrganisationMeasure".

item 2 measure concerns the service interop 1.

item 2 measure has the description "Assess the organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services deliveryPlease list the governance measures foreseen".


item 3 barrier is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/3/barrier".

item 3 barrier is an assessment statement.

item 3 barrier has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationNegative".

item 3 barrier has the judgement "-The specific data sources that the legislation aims to reuse may not use harmonised concepts andthegranularity of observations may hinder the reuse of data for the purpose of statistics;
-iplementation aspects may involve the creation of additional vocabularies.".

item 3 barrier has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeSharedBarrier".

item 3 barrier concerns the service interop 1.

item 3 barrier has the description "Assess the measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the dataPlease list such measures".


item 3 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/3/measure".

item 3 measure is an assessment statement.

item 3 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 3 measure has the judgement "-Promotes the use of international standards for fisheries statistics, including concepts and classifications,such as the Fishing Areas for Statistical Purposes and the ASFISlist ofspecies.
-Promotes the alignment of the data requests, definitions, methodologies, and reporting formats with those oftheFAO and theOECD.
-Promotes the use of a clear definition for ‘aquaculture establishments’.
-Applies Regulation (EC) No1059/2003 of the European Parliament and of the Council to data on terrestrial units.".

item 3 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeSharedMeasure".

item 3 measure concerns the service interop 1.

item 3 measure has the description "Assess the measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the dataPlease list such measures".


item 4 barrier is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/4/barrier".

item 4 barrier is an assessment statement.

item 4 barrier has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationNegative".

item 4 barrier has the judgement "-Further developments are neededtoextract anddevelopthe data thatarecurrently stored in internal Commission repositories.".

item 4 barrier has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeStandardsBarrier".

item 4 barrier concerns the service interop 1.

item 4 barrier has the description "Assess the use of commonly agreed open technical specifications and standardsPlease list such measures".


